edit(n,10,'Making a published extensible class final breaks clients.',j,lambda q:(opt(q,1,text='For new APIs, make classes final unless designed for extension; migrate existing subclassing clients before closing an API'),fields(q,workedExample=q['workedExample'].replace('Final by default: no subclasses, no dependence.','For new APIs, final by default prevents new subclass dependencies. Retrofitting final on a published superclass is a breaking change.'))))
edit(n,11,'Megamorphic inlining outcome not absolute; dependent on JIT/version/profile.',j,lambda q:(opt(q,3,text='A monomorphic site may allow guarded inlining of Circle.area; a diverse receiver profile can make useful inlining harder and retain indirect dispatch',explanation='Correct. This is an optimization opportunity, not a guaranteed performance outcome. HotSpot decisions depend on profile, method size, compiler and version.'),fields(q,workedExample='HotSpot profiles receiver types. A monomorphic site may inline the observed implementation with a guard or another valid type assumption. A diverse receiver profile can reduce profitable inlining opportunities, leaving indirect dispatch and fewer downstream optimizations. Some polymorphic sites can still inline targets; six classes does not impose a universal ban. Measure the actual compiled workload.')))
